 "duration_s": 28.48,
 "script": "The helmet clicks onto your head, while tiny sensors around the cockpit start tracking exactly where it points. A display inside the visor paints target boxes over the real sky, and the jet's computer knows every direction you look. When you turn your head toward an enemy plane, the missile's seeker swings to match your gaze, locking on even when the target is beside you, not ahead. Now, if you wore this helmet in Bengaluru traffic, you could lock onto every gap between the lanes, plotting your escape before an auto-rickshaw takes it first.",
